---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import { KnowledgeBasePlayground } from '../../components/KnowledgeBaseDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Knowledge Base" description="Which sources feed a knowledge base, and how each sync is going.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Knowledge Base</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A panel for the apps a knowledge base reads from, such as Slack, GitHub, and Jira. Each source draws a line into the
    index as it syncs, and the list beside it says what is connected, syncing, paused, or failed.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8 flex justify-center">
    <KnowledgeBasePlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Knowledge Base usage"
      code={`import { Button } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button";
import {
  KnowledgeBase,
  KnowledgeBaseActivity,
  KnowledgeBaseDiagram,
  KnowledgeBaseFooter,
  KnowledgeBaseHeader,
  KnowledgeBaseSources,
  KnowledgeBaseSummary,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/knowledge-base";

<KnowledgeBase
  sources={[
    { id: "slack", name: "Slack", brand: "slack", detail: "#support · live", status: "connected", chunks: 1284, newChunks: 36 },
    { id: "github", name: "GitHub", brand: "github", detail: "acme/platform", status: "syncing", progress: 40, chunks: 380 },
    { id: "jira", name: "Jira", brand: "jira", status: "error", error: "Token expired. Reconnect to resume." },
    { id: "notion", name: "Notion", brand: "notion", status: "available" },
  ]}
>
  <KnowledgeBaseHeader subtitle="Acme Assist" />
  <KnowledgeBaseDiagram mark={<YourLogo />}>
    <KnowledgeBaseActivity />
  </KnowledgeBaseDiagram>
  <KnowledgeBaseSummary>
    <Button size="sm">Upload files</Button>
  </KnowledgeBaseSummary>
  <KnowledgeBaseSources
    connectHref={source => \`/integrations/\${source.id}\`}
    onRetry={retry}
    onSync={sync}
    onPauseSync={pause}
    onResumeSync={resume}
    onCancelSync={cancel}
    onSettings={openSettings}
    onDisconnect={disconnect}
  />
  <KnowledgeBaseFooter />
</KnowledgeBase>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>KnowledgeBaseSource</code>: <code>{'{ id, name, brand, icon, detail, status }'}</code>, plus
        <code>progress</code>, <code>chunks</code>, <code>newChunks</code>, <code>error</code>, and
        <code>color</code>. <code>newChunks</code> shows as “+36 new” beside the count. <code>error</code> replaces the
        detail on a failed source.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>KnowledgeBaseDiagram</code>: <code>mark</code> is your logo, laid on top of the index, such as an
        <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> with a <code>viewBox</code>. It defaults to a document outline. Children float over the
        stage's top-left corner.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>KnowledgeBaseActivity</code>: a small readout of what is indexed. It shows a spinner while sources sync,
        the chunk and source counts, and the chunks the latest syncs added. With nothing linked it reads “Nothing
        indexed”. Counts roll up as they change.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>KnowledgeBaseSources</code>: <code>onConnect</code> shows Connect on available sources;
        <code>connectHref</code> makes it a link instead, such as to the integration's setup page, and wins over
        <code>onConnect</code>. <code>onRetry</code> shows Retry on failed sources. The row menu holds
        <code>onSync</code> (“Sync now”), <code>onPauseSync</code> (“Pause syncing”), <code>onResumeSync</code>
        (“Resume syncing”), <code>onCancelSync</code> (“Cancel sync”), <code>onSettings</code>, and
        <code>onDisconnect</code>. Each item appears only for the statuses it fits. Rows without a menu keep its space,
        so statuses line up.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      A source is <code>available</code>, <code>queued</code>, <code>syncing</code> (with <code>progress</code> from 0
      to 100), <code>connected</code>, <code>paused</code>, or <code>error</code>. The panel works out its own state
      from them: empty, syncing, attention, partial, or ready. The summary heading, its sentence, and the footer follow
      it unless you pass <code>title</code> or <code>description</code>. The diagram shows up to six sources; the rest
      are counted on the last tile, syncing and failed sources first.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Motion</h2>
    <p>
      A syncing source's line draws toward the index as its progress grows, with data moving along it, and its share of
      the embedding dots lights up. Connected lines hold still and send one packet every few seconds. Failed lines turn
      red and dashed. With reduced motion, lines and dots change without moving and no packets run.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The diagram is hidden from screen readers; the list carries the same facts as text, and every status has a word,
      not only a color. Syncing rows are progress bars. Buttons name their source, such as “Connect Slack”. A polite
      live region reads out sources as they finish or fail.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The panel uses <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, and <code>--sprout-radius-panel</code>.
      Each line takes its app's own color, such as Slack's or Jira's, and black marks like GitHub follow the text color.
      On dark surfaces, brand colors mix toward the text color by
      <code>--sprout-knowledge-base-brand-mix</code> so deep blues stay visible. Sources without a brand take
      categorical hues (<code>--sprout-sky</code>, <code>--sprout-teal</code>, …). Pass <code>color</code> on a source
      to choose its own. <code>--sprout-knowledge-base-stage</code> sets the diagram background.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
